# Unified Session Status Coloring

This plan ensures consistent and clear coloring for session statuses (Holiday, Teacher Absence, and Substitute Teacher) across the Daily Sessions Calendar and the Yearly Performance Radar.

## Color Scheme Specification

| Status | Color (Light) | Color (Dark/Midnight) | Icon/Marker |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Holiday (عطلة)** | Blue (`bg-blue-100/50` border `blue-300`) | `bg-blue-900/40` border `blue-800` | 🏝️ |
| **Teacher Absent (غياب الشيخ)** | Red (`bg-red-50` border `red-200`) | `bg-red-950/30` border `red-800` | ❌ |
| **Substitute Teacher (شيخ بديل)** | Purple (`bg-purple-50` border `purple-200`) | `bg-purple-950/30` border `purple-800` | 🔄 |
| **Normal Session (حصة عادية)** | Green (`bg-emerald-50` border `emerald-200`) | `bg-emerald-900/40` border `emerald-800` | ✅ |

## Proposed Changes

### [Component] Session Components
#### [MODIFY] [SessionCalendar.tsx](file:///g:/Al-Shafi-i-Group-main/Al-Shafi-i-Group-main/src/components/sessions/SessionCalendar.tsx)
- Update `statusClass` logic to differentiate between:
  - Holiday (Blue)
  - Sheikh Absent without substitute (Red)
  - Sheikh Absent with substitute (Purple)
  - Normal session (Green)
- Ensure colors are consistent with the "Classic" (light) theme requirements.

### [Page] Analytics Layer
#### [MODIFY] [yearly-performance/page.tsx](file:///g:/Al-Shafi-i-Group-main/Al-Shafi-i-Group-main/src/app/yearly-performance/page.tsx)
- Update [getDayColor](file:///g:/Al-Shafi-i-Group-main/Al-Shafi-i-Group-main/src/app/yearly-performance/page.tsx#15-24) helper function to match the new color scheme.
- Update `yearlyData` memo logic to properly flag "Absent with Substitute".
- Update the legend (bottom of the page) to reflect the new categories.
- Ensure the tooltip content reflects these statuses accurately.

## Verification Plan
### Automated Tests
- N/A (Visual styling changes)

### Manual Verification
1. Create a session of each type (Normal, Holiday, Absent, Absent with Substitute).
2. Verify colors in the Daily Sessions Calendar (Light and Dark themes).
3. Verify colors in the Yearly Performance Radar (Light and Dark themes).
4. Check that tooltips in the Radar show the correct status names.
